[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5333968791","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122554#issuecomment-5333968791","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122554","id":5333968791,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPe3nlw","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-18T20:57:16Z","updated_at":"2026-08-18T22:40:47Z","body":"- Related to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109639 (since it only happens when moving the mouse).\n\nI can confirm this on 4.8.dev3 (Windows 11 24H2, 240 Hz display, 1000 Hz mouse polling rate). On average, it occurs after 3-4 attempts:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/05668b4e-dcaf-4496-ab22-305277cb57e6\n\nI couldn't reproduce this on 4.7.1.stable, which doesn't include https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109639.\n\n**Edit:** I bisected the regression to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109639.\n\ncc @bruvzg @vorvek ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5333968791/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5335051176","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122554#issuecomment-5335051176","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122554","id":5335051176,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPf5rqA","user":{"login":"vorvek","id":9655848,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTU4NDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9655848?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek","html_url":"https://github.com/vorvek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-18T22:46:11Z","updated_at":"2026-08-18T22:46:11Z","body":"My hypothesis is that #109639 moved raw-input draining ahead of the normal Windows message pump. A raw Shift-up can thus be converted into a release event before older queued WM_KEYDOWN repeated messages are dispatched, producing this sequence: release, echoed press. Mouse traffic makes that backlog/order inversion easier to happen.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5335051176/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5337567804","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122554#issuecomment-5337567804","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122554","id":5337567804,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPiTSPA","user":{"login":"DreamyCecil","id":21009796,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDA5Nzk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21009796?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamyCecil","html_url":"https://github.com/DreamyCecil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamyCecil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamyCecil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamyCecil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamyCecil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamyCecil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamyCecil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamyCecil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamyCecil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamyCecil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-19T04:33:36Z","updated_at":"2026-08-19T04:34:18Z","body":"I have encountered the same issue in my project after updating from 4.7.1 to 4.7.2 (both Mono builds for C#) and at first I couldn't pin down the exact cause for the Shift key sometimes getting stuck (both left and right) but I eventually narrowed down how to successfully reproduce it every single time:\n1. Start holding Shift\n2. Start holding Num 0\n3. Release Shift\n\nThis makes the Shift key stuck every single time like it was never released, even after releasing Num 0.\n\nSome strange thing also happens with the example code from the issue, which produces the following results, which I hope will be helpful:\n- Holding Shift spams \"**Shift Pressed true**\" in the console until I tap Num 0, which results in \"**Shift Released**\" and \"**Shift Pressed false**\" to be printed, which stops the initial message spam, as if I stopped holding Shift (which is still pressed). Releasing it after it just adds an extra \"**Shift Released**\":\n```\n// Start holding Shift\n...\nShift Pressed true\nShift Pressed true\nShift Pressed true\n// Press and release Num 0\nShift Released\nShift Pressed false\n// Stop holding shift\nShift Released\n```\n- Holding Shift spams \"**Shift Pressed true**\" in the console until I start holding Num 0 and then release Shift, which results in two \"**Shift Released**\" and one \"**Shift Pressed false**\" to be printed. Releasing Num 0 doesn't do anything extra:\n```\n// Start holding Shift\n...\nShift Pressed true\nShift Pressed true\n// Start holding Num 0\n// Stop holding Shift\nShift Released\nShift Released\nShift Pressed false\n// Stop holding Num 0\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5337567804/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5340634094","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122554#issuecomment-5340634094","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122554","id":5340634094,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPlOb7g","user":{"login":"vorvek","id":9655848,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTU4NDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9655848?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek","html_url":"https://github.com/vorvek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-19T10:10:25Z","updated_at":"2026-08-19T10:20:29Z","body":"The thing is, shift + a numpad number replaces the input message in Windows. Shift + Num 1 is \"End\", Shift + Num 7 is 'Home', and so on. The behavior can potentially be changed, but I don't think it's a bug per se.\n\nThis is how the message queue looks:\n\n```\nWM_KEYDOWN  VK_SHIFT   scan=2A  asyncL=True\nWM_KEYUP    VK_SHIFT   scan=2A  asyncL=False  <- after Numpad0 down,\nWM_KEYDOWN  VK_INSERT  scan=52                   before physical Shift-up\n```\n\nSo, we would need to decide whether we go with normal Windows behaviour or with the actual physical state of the keyboard. \n\nSources:\nhttps://devblogs.microsoft.com/oldnewthing/20040906-00/?p=37953\nhttps://devblogs.microsoft.com/oldnewthing/20260212-00/?p=112059","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5340634094/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5347167305","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122554#issuecomment-5347167305","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122554","id":5347167305,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPrdMSQ","user":{"login":"DreamyCecil","id":21009796,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDA5Nzk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21009796?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamyCecil","html_url":"https://github.com/DreamyCecil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamyCecil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamyCecil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamyCecil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamyCecil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamyCecil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamyCecil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamyCecil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamyCecil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DreamyCecil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-19T19:45:32Z","updated_at":"2026-08-19T19:46:15Z","body":"I can use either button for their respective actions in-game (separately or simultaneously, which sometimes results in Shift getting stuck) because I have Num Lock toggled on. It worked perfectly fine on 4.7.1 and works in any other game I've ever played if I rebound the keys to Shift and Num 0 and used both of them for whatever.\n\nDidn't know holding Shift allowed for the alternate actions to work as I've never used the numpad this way. I thought the alternate actions only worked with Num Lock toggled off.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5347167305/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5372753677","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122554#issuecomment-5372753677","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122554","id":5372753677,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQD23DQ","user":{"login":"HarDevSan","id":49758694,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NzU4Njk0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49758694?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HarDevSan","html_url":"https://github.com/HarDevSan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HarDevSan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HarDevSan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HarDevSan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HarDevSan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HarDevSan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HarDevSan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HarDevSan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HarDevSan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HarDevSan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-21T16:51:07Z","updated_at":"2026-08-21T16:51:07Z","body":"I just wanted to say thank you for this issue. I would have not in a million years guessed this was an engine problem and I already started going nuts. Reverted to 4.7.1 in the meantime. Crossing fingers the fix could be delivered for 4.7. still, not just for 4.8, since I am working on a project and would not really like to have to jump major versions again to avoid this, with most of my used plugins falling behind again. Thanks a lot for your work.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5372753677/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]